WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:08.620
Cut every nerve to a loop of a dog's gut, then drip weak acid onto its lining.

2
00:00:09.380 --> 00:00:11.600
The pancreas still secretes its juice.

3
00:00:12.220 --> 00:00:16.300
It sits in a different part of the abdomen, and the leading view said the gut

4
00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:17.660
instructs it by nerve.

5
00:00:18.360 --> 00:00:20.860
But no wire joins the two organs now.

6
00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:22.840
What carried the message?

7
00:00:23.683 --> 00:00:26.683
The answer was a chemical, later named secretin.

8
00:00:27.283 --> 00:00:31.023
Acid released it from the gut lining, and the blood carried it to the pancreas.

9
00:00:31.463 --> 00:00:36.183
An extract of the lining, filtered and injected into a vein, made the pancreas

10
00:00:36.183 --> 00:00:37.323
secrete even more.

11
00:00:37.843 --> 00:00:40.123
But molecules can also drift on their own.

12
00:00:40.603 --> 00:00:42.123
So why ride the blood at all?

13
00:00:42.983 --> 00:00:44.583
That drift is called diffusion.

14
00:00:45.303 --> 00:00:47.363
A diffusing molecule is not heading anywhere.

15
00:00:47.883 --> 00:00:52.803
It wanders. The typical time to wander a distance grows with the square of that

16
00:00:52.803 --> 00:00:58.583
distance. So diffusion punishes distance: a far target waits much longer than a near

17
00:00:58.583 --> 00:00:59.583
one.

18
00:00:59.683 --> 00:01:03.323
Take a small molecule in water, and change only the distance.

19
00:01:04.003 --> 00:01:09.183
It crosses a synaptic gap, 20 nanometers wide, in a fraction of a microsecond.

20
00:01:09.823 --> 00:01:12.103
It crosses a millimeter in about 8 minutes.

21
00:01:12.623 --> 00:01:15.403
It crosses a centimeter in about 14 hours.

22
00:01:16.003 --> 00:01:20.403
The centimeter is only 10 times farther than the millimeter, yet it costs hours

23
00:01:20.403 --> 00:01:21.403
instead of minutes.

24
00:01:22.217 --> 00:01:26.737
Past a few hundred micrometers, diffusion cannot deliver a message that must act

25
00:01:26.737 --> 00:01:31.317
within a minute. So a gland releases its hormone into the blood, which circulates

26
00:01:31.317 --> 00:01:32.937
around the body in about a minute.

27
00:01:33.817 --> 00:01:35.477
Fast local signals do the opposite.

28
00:01:36.137 --> 00:01:40.357
A nerve cell releases its message into a gap only tens of nanometers wide.

29
00:01:40.937 --> 00:01:44.737
The message arrives almost at once, though some spills out to nearby cells.

30
00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:50.120
The extract reached every organ in the dog, and the pancreas poured out juice.

31
00:01:50.820 --> 00:01:52.480
A signal does not choose its audience.

32
00:01:53.020 --> 00:01:54.020
The receiver does.

33
00:01:54.500 --> 00:02:00.020
Epinephrine, a hormone, makes liver cells break down glycogen, fat cells break down

34
00:02:00.020 --> 00:02:01.940
fat, and the heart beat harder.

35
00:02:02.480 --> 00:02:07.880
So keep this rule: far messages ride the blood, and the receptor decides who

36
00:02:07.880 --> 00:02:08.280
answers.
